Downloads the remote outputs of a completed run to the local file system.

This is useful for runs on a cloud backend (e.g. TES), where the output files remain in remote storage after the run completes.

Usage: sprocket localize [OPTIONS] <RUN>

Arguments:
  <RUN>
          The run whose outputs should be localized.

          This may be the path to a run directory (e.g. `out/runs/<target>/<timestamp>` or `out/runs/<target>/_latest`) or the path to the `outputs.json` file inside of one.

          Note that `outputs.json` does not record the WDL type of each output, so any string output that is a remote storage URL (`s3://`, `az://`, `gs://`, `http://`, or `https://`) is treated as a remote file or directory.

Options:
  -d, --destination <DESTINATION>
          The directory to download the outputs into.

          Defaults to `localized` within the run directory.

          Each remote output is downloaded to `<DESTINATION>/<output name>/<file or directory name>`. A localized copy of `outputs.json` that refers to the downloaded files is written to `<DESTINATION>/outputs.json`.

      --overwrite
          Overwrite files that already exist in the destination

      --dry-run
          Show what would be downloaded without downloading anything

      --azure-account-name <NAME>
          The Azure Storage account name to use

          [env: AZURE_ACCOUNT_NAME=]

      --azure-access-key <KEY>
          The Azure Storage access key to use

          [env: AZURE_ACCESS_KEY]

      --aws-access-key-id <ID>
          The AWS Access Key ID to use; overrides configuration

          [env: AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=]

      --aws-secret-access-key <KEY>
          The AWS Secret Access Key to use; overrides configuration

          [env: AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY]

      --aws-default-region <REGION>
          The default AWS region; overrides configuration

          [env: AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=]

      --google-hmac-access-key <KEY>
          The Google Cloud Storage HMAC access key to use; overrides configuration

          [env: GOOGLE_HMAC_ACCESS_KEY=]

      --google-hmac-secret <SECRET>
          The Google Cloud Storage HMAC secret to use; overrides configuration

          [env: GOOGLE_HMAC_SECRET]

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

      --no-ignore
          Ignore `.sprocketignore` files while discovering WDL documents

      --color <COLOR>
          Controls output colorization

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Automatically colorize output depending on output device
          - always: Always colorize output
          - never:  Never colorize output

          [default: auto]

  -m, --report-mode <MODE>
          The report mode for any emitted diagnostics

          Possible values:
          - full:     Prints diagnostics as multiple lines
          - one-line: Prints diagnostics as one line

  -c, --config <CONFIG>
          Path to the configuration file

  -s, --skip-config-search
          Skip searching for and loading configuration files.

          Only a configuration file specified as a command line argument will be used.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
